WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:03.750
- [Mark] All right, Johnny what
are we talkin' about today?

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:04.583
- Here we go.

00:00:04.583 --> 00:00:05.416
We gonna talk about a little bit.

00:00:05.416 --> 00:00:06.249
I talk a lot,

00:00:06.249 --> 00:00:07.610
in my interviews I talk a lot about

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:08.840
being down here in Los Angeles.

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:10.400
You know, me running around in the hood.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:11.740
Runnin' around down here in downtown LA.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:13.000
You know, different parts of LA.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.200
But I've never shared, you know,

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:16.250
when I went outta state.

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:17.584
You know what I mean?

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:18.417
When I was about 15 years old

00:00:18.417 --> 00:00:19.890
this musta been, oo man,

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:23.800
I'd say '87, '88 maybe.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:26.080
I was about 15 years old and
it was gettin' hot down here.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:27.150
You know.

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:28.750
MC Texas kept comin' to the house.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:30.150
You know what I mean?

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.040
They kept raidin' the house for my uncle.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:33.540
And kept raidin' the house
for my brother, you know.

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.750
So, it was becoming too
hot at the house, you know.

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:36.670
Every time they raided it,

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:37.869
they'd just take me to jail

00:00:37.869 --> 00:00:38.702
and let me out in a few hours

00:00:38.702 --> 00:00:40.230
but I didn't like the feeling.

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:41.310
So, I got my Grandmother,

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:44.460
and I told her, you know,
I wanna go to Mexico.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:45.760
And she said, I already
sent you over there.

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:47.003
You know what I mean?

00:00:47.003 --> 00:00:47.836
I already went over there.

00:00:47.836 --> 00:00:48.669
I wanted to go back.

00:00:48.669 --> 00:00:49.502
Well, she didn't wanna send me.

00:00:49.502 --> 00:00:50.335
So, she said, well,

00:00:50.335 --> 00:00:51.300
why don't we send you to
Arizona for a little while,

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.770
you know, with some people up there?

00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:55.210
And I was like, all right,
at least check it out.

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:56.462
You know what I mean?

00:00:56.462 --> 00:00:57.295
Lets go.

00:00:57.295 --> 00:00:58.128
You know, it was,

00:00:58.128 --> 00:00:59.540
the summer was gone, so I was
figurin' it's not that hot.

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:01.607
Still, I got there and it
was fuckin' boiling hot

00:01:01.607 --> 00:01:03.220
and we're in the middle of October.

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:05.450
Like, right now, in here it's boiling hot.

00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:07.440
You know, I got there and

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:08.810
you know, the school year was passing

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:10.120
and I wanted to get enrolled in school

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:11.990
'cause I just didn't
wanna run around there,

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:13.750
have the cops or the
truant officer catch me

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:16.190
because, remember I went there by myself.

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:18.130
Low and behold, what I did was,

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:19.180
I got some money together,

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:20.170
I got my clothes together

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:22.250
and I went to the bus depot.

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:23.320
Not this one.

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:24.360
The old bus depot.

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:27.600
The one that use to be on 7th and Maple.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:28.850
Around,

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:29.683
yeah, right there on 7th and Maple,

00:01:29.683 --> 00:01:30.516
the old bus depot.

00:01:30.516 --> 00:01:31.800
So, I went over there

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:33.770
and I remember when I got there, you know,

00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:35.610
some fool snatched my luggage real fast.

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:37.240
Man, I thought he was
tryin' to steal my shit,

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:38.567
so I gave chase to him.

00:01:38.567 --> 00:01:40.690
And he's like, hey, hey,
I'm just helpin' you out.

00:01:40.690 --> 00:01:42.380
You know, I didn't know
that there was dudes

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:44.400
that would help you take your
luggage wherever it gots to go

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:46.730
and you know, break 'em off,
whatever, change your dollars.

00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:47.740
I thought he was robbing me.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:48.573
You know, I'm young.

00:01:48.573 --> 00:01:49.879
15.

00:01:49.879 --> 00:01:50.712
He's grabbin' my suitcases.

00:01:50.712 --> 00:01:51.545
He's a grown man.

00:01:51.545 --> 00:01:52.550
I'm like, man, I get at him.

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:53.770
Anyways, I gave him some change.

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:54.970
I get on the bus.

00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:58.050
So, on the way to Arizona,

00:01:58.050 --> 00:01:59.330
we're like halfway there

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:00.860
and all the sudden,

00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:03.780
the bus pulls over to
the side of the road.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:05.650
And then I see sirens, you know,

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:06.810
flashing in the windows.

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:08.680
And I'm like, oh shit.

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:10.110
They pull over the fuckin' bus.

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:12.160
Oh man, I hope they didn't fuckin' see me

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:13.300
or you know, they're lookin' for me.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:15.110
So, I'm thinkin' it's all about me.

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:16.380
Nah, they got on the bus

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.960
and took this man and this little kid off.

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:20.090
Then took them both, you know.

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:21.160
So, it was cool.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:23.810
But I was already bustin'
out my pictures that I took,

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:25.210
you know, me in LA and stuff,

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:26.510
just in case, you know,

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:27.802
'cause I don't got no ID.

00:02:27.802 --> 00:02:28.635
You know what I mean?

00:02:28.635 --> 00:02:29.550
And a lot of times right there

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:32.890
in that part of the trip to Arizona,

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:34.831
they deport people.

00:02:34.831 --> 00:02:37.020
That's by Coachella, Indio, all that area.

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:38.210
They deport a lot of people.

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:39.043
You know what I mean?

00:02:39.043 --> 00:02:40.700
And they catch you on the bus by yourself,

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:42.200
no ID, nothing, no one with you,

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:43.170
of course, they're gonna take you.

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:44.003
You know what I mean?

00:02:44.003 --> 00:02:45.250
Well, they bypass me.

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:46.083
Cool.

00:02:46.083 --> 00:02:48.000
I went all they way to Arizona.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:48.973
When I got there,

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:51.040
I got there, it was about,

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:52.430
oo, it was late at night.

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:54.391
So, I went, you know what I mean?

00:02:54.391 --> 00:02:55.224
Went in the backyard, kicked it.

00:02:55.224 --> 00:02:56.700
They got a spot out there.

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:57.533
Kicked it in the backyard.

00:02:57.533 --> 00:02:58.366
Wait til the next day.

00:02:58.366 --> 00:02:59.199
The next day came.

00:02:59.199 --> 00:03:00.980
I was like, okay, what
am I gonna do over here?

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.510
You know, I could be sellin' drugs.

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:03.343
You know what I mean?

00:03:03.343 --> 00:03:04.610
Outta my Grandma's house.

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:05.443
I could just run wild right here.

00:03:05.443 --> 00:03:08.372
Or I could enroll in school
and see what that's like.

00:03:08.372 --> 00:03:09.205
You know?

00:03:09.205 --> 00:03:10.038
I'm only 15,

00:03:10.038 --> 00:03:11.523
so I go to one of my aunts and I'm like,

00:03:11.523 --> 00:03:12.910
hey, can you enroll me in school?

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:13.840
She didn't wanna do it,

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:16.180
so my cousin, she ended up doin' it.

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:17.100
They enrolled me in school,

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:18.420
put my Grandmother's address.

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:20.270
Now I'm goin' to school, right.

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:21.697
I'm goin' to school there

00:03:21.697 --> 00:03:22.920
and it's,

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:24.720
it's similar to back home

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:25.940
but it's just a lot slower.

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:27.284
You know what I mean?

00:03:27.284 --> 00:03:29.010
They ain't doing as much shit.

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:29.843
They're doin' it on the low

00:03:29.843 --> 00:03:30.676
but they're not doin'

00:03:30.676 --> 00:03:32.430
as much shit as we're doin' back in LA.

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:34.990
You know, they're about
three gears back, you know.

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:36.550
But one time I'm kickin' it,

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:37.736
you know what I mean?

00:03:37.736 --> 00:03:38.569
And I was watchin' this dude.

00:03:38.569 --> 00:03:40.470
You know, he was Mexican and Puerto Rican.

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:42.270
He lived across the street from me

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:44.100
and I always use to see him at night

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:45.297
comin' back at night.

00:03:45.297 --> 00:03:46.670
You know, I'm wonderin' what
the fuck is this dude up to.

00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:47.710
You know, so,

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:48.950
one time he walks by.

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:49.783
I call him.

00:03:49.783 --> 00:03:50.780
And we smoke a cigarette.

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:52.290
We get to know each other.

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:54.470
Low and behold, I know
this dudes a robber.

00:03:54.470 --> 00:03:56.200
You know, he robs all kinds of shit.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:57.290
You know what I mean?

00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:58.650
I'm down there with him and I'm sayin',

00:03:58.650 --> 00:03:59.610
fuck it, let's go.

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:00.480
Let's go for a whirl.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:01.770
You know, see what's up.

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:03.052
He goes, well, I'll be back.

00:04:03.052 --> 00:04:03.885
Right now I gotta go get something.

00:04:03.885 --> 00:04:04.718
So, he leaves.

00:04:04.718 --> 00:04:05.551
He comes back.

00:04:05.551 --> 00:04:06.384
When he comes back,

00:04:06.384 --> 00:04:07.490
he has this,

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:09.430
I gotta be that year,

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:10.540
a Ford truck.

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:11.373
A big one.

00:04:11.373 --> 00:04:12.680
King cab.

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:13.840
A long bed.

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:17.180
I'm talkin' about high as
truck and bad mother fucker.

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:18.550
Four wheel drive, everything, right.

00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:19.850
It looks brand new.

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:21.446
So, I'm like where'd
you get this truck at?

00:04:21.446 --> 00:04:23.360
And he was like, man, I
just went to the car lot,

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:24.740
by the side of the office, man.

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:25.573
Open the shit.

00:04:25.573 --> 00:04:26.406
All the keys were hangin'.

00:04:26.406 --> 00:04:28.040
I grab the key, got in it and took off.

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:30.220
I'm like, yeah, but
there's poles and chains.

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:31.053
He goes, nah, man.

00:04:31.053 --> 00:04:31.886
He goes, I'll show you.

00:04:31.886 --> 00:04:33.160
He took me over there and it's straight

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:37.850
because all those used car
lots always have one pole

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:41.020
that comes up and then you
can lay it on the ground.

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:41.960
And that lays the chain out.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:43.040
You know, I never knew that.

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:44.630
I never knew that til he showed me.

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:45.603
So, we went over there.

00:04:45.603 --> 00:04:47.530
When we took the pole out, laid it down,

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:48.450
went inside the office.

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:49.900
He went inside, pulled all the keys out.

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:51.237
We're all looking the keys

00:04:51.237 --> 00:04:54.060
and boom I see this nice ass Trans Am.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.900
I'm like, oh, I'll take the Trans Am.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:56.733
It's blocked in.

00:04:56.733 --> 00:04:58.330
So, I'm like, okay, we
gotta move the white truck.

00:04:58.330 --> 00:04:59.910
And you know, what it is,

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:02.310
it's just a, you know, a set like this,

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:04.530
a set which is a gang of keys in there

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:07.500
and they all have what year,
what color, what model.

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:09.230
So, you just look at
the car lot, get the key

00:05:09.230 --> 00:05:11.050
and boom, presto, you
know, you got the car,

00:05:11.050 --> 00:05:12.732
so, we ended up getting

00:05:12.732 --> 00:05:14.280
about three or four that night.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:15.210
Now, we're cruisin' around.

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:17.100
We're wonderin' where we gonna take 'em.

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:18.960
So, I said, you know what?

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:20.150
We could wait til the morning

00:05:20.150 --> 00:05:21.360
and then we could drive to Mexico.

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:23.450
I mean, and Mexico's only 13 miles.

00:05:23.450 --> 00:05:25.620
So, I figured, the worst
that could happen is

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:27.090
we gotta walk back.

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:28.700
To me, that's the worst that could happen.

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:29.533
So, we go.

00:05:29.533 --> 00:05:30.720
There's about five of us.

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:32.070
We go in about three cars.

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:33.510
We go there with a truck and two cars.

00:05:33.510 --> 00:05:34.410
We go over there.

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:37.500
We meet some dude, we met
on this side over here.

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:39.560
He's talkin' about his aunts
and everything live right there

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:40.900
and they did.

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:43.830
And they wanna buy all the
cars as soon as we get there.

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:46.210
So, we got there and
we stay a little while.

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:47.120
We went an partied with dude.

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:48.640
We went deeper into Mexico.

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:51.043
We went to the border of,

00:05:51.043 --> 00:05:52.090
it's called Al de Lones.

00:05:52.090 --> 00:05:57.090
It's in between San Louis,
Mexico and Chicale, like that.

00:05:58.330 --> 00:05:59.680
Yeah, Mexicali or one of those.

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:00.513
It's right in the middle.

00:06:00.513 --> 00:06:01.840
It's a little ass border.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:03.800
It's got like, one car goes in,

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:04.633
one car goes out.

00:06:04.633 --> 00:06:05.660
Small ass border,

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:06.493
by the canyons.

00:06:06.493 --> 00:06:08.700
You gotta drive along the
Colorado to get there.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:09.630
You know what I mean?

00:06:09.630 --> 00:06:10.720
It's a small ass border.

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:13.380
So, we get there and we
rolled through like nothin'.

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:14.920
Boom, we rolled through.

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:16.395
And at first when we
get there, dudes like,

00:06:16.395 --> 00:06:17.370
come on let's go to the bar, you know.

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:19.700
And I didn't know that
you could be any age

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:20.620
to drink in Mexico.

00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:22.172
You just gotta act right.

00:06:22.172 --> 00:06:23.005
You know what I mean?

00:06:23.005 --> 00:06:23.838
If you act a fool, they're
gonna take you to jail.

00:06:23.838 --> 00:06:24.671
You're fucked.

00:06:24.671 --> 00:06:25.504
But if you act right, you know,

00:06:25.504 --> 00:06:27.380
you can have women sitting on your lap.

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:28.590
I had a woman sitting on my lap.

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:29.423
I was 15.

00:06:29.423 --> 00:06:30.559
You know what I mean?

00:06:30.559 --> 00:06:31.392
I was buyin' rounds, buyin' rounds

00:06:31.392 --> 00:06:33.430
'cause, you know, over
there, like 20 bucks, man,

00:06:33.430 --> 00:06:36.040
will buy you like seven rounds in a bar.

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:37.670
You know, with everybody there.

00:06:37.670 --> 00:06:38.906
So, we're buyin' shit.

00:06:38.906 --> 00:06:39.880
We're buyin' shit.

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:41.110
My uncle walks in.

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:41.943
Boom.

00:06:41.943 --> 00:06:42.776
My grandfather's brother.

00:06:42.776 --> 00:06:44.460
I'm thinkin', oh shit, man,

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:45.293
I'm through with wonderin' this.

00:06:45.293 --> 00:06:46.610
Who's gonna tell.

00:06:46.610 --> 00:06:47.443
Nah.

00:06:47.443 --> 00:06:48.710
He said, what's up.

00:06:48.710 --> 00:06:49.543
How you doin', man.

00:06:49.543 --> 00:06:50.376
Grabbed himself two broads,

00:06:50.376 --> 00:06:51.310
sat 'em on his lap.

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:52.513
And then started partyin'.

00:06:52.513 --> 00:06:53.346
And then I was like, okay.

00:06:53.346 --> 00:06:54.200
So, he ain't gonna tell on me.

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:56.020
So, we went over there and we had,

00:06:56.020 --> 00:07:00.300
okay, they dude told us that
we were gonna get 2500 a truck

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:02.920
and 2,000 a car.

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:04.680
Now, you know, when you get somewhere,

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:06.030
always in the deal,
when you get somewhere,

00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:07.660
a mother fucker wants to change it up.

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:08.493
We're in Mexico.

00:07:08.493 --> 00:07:09.326
What could we say?

00:07:09.326 --> 00:07:10.504
You know what I mean?

00:07:10.504 --> 00:07:11.337
He's tryin' to short change us like 2,000.

00:07:11.337 --> 00:07:13.504
But what could we say, we're in Mexico.

00:07:13.504 --> 00:07:14.337
You know what I mean?

00:07:14.337 --> 00:07:15.960
Once we're over here, we got no backing.

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:17.360
I'm all the way in LA.

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:19.260
Where we're at in Arizona,
that's 13 miles away,

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:20.750
so I'm like, damn, this
fool's gonna get us.

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:21.610
Fuck it.

00:07:21.610 --> 00:07:22.740
We told him, yeah, yeah, whatever.

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:23.870
So, we got it.

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:25.070
We put the money in our pockets.

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:26.660
Now, remember, we're there all day.

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:29.150
What happened was, we lost track of time.

00:07:29.150 --> 00:07:31.960
The border closes at
eight o'clock exactly.

00:07:31.960 --> 00:07:33.843
It's like 10 til eight.

00:07:34.844 --> 00:07:35.737
So, we're like, fuck.

00:07:35.737 --> 00:07:37.410
We got no chance of
gettin' a car or nothin'.

00:07:37.410 --> 00:07:38.720
We gotta run.

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:39.630
So, we run, man.

00:07:39.630 --> 00:07:40.810
We run.

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:44.000
We get there, it's like
five minutes to close.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:44.833
We get there.

00:07:44.833 --> 00:07:46.030
We go through.

00:07:46.030 --> 00:07:46.863
Boom, boom, boom, with our money.

00:07:46.863 --> 00:07:49.570
Now, we're stuck and
we got 13 miles to walk

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:50.403
along the Colorado.

00:07:50.403 --> 00:07:53.230
Now, 13 miles is a long time
when you ain't got no water.

00:07:53.230 --> 00:07:55.150
It's a fuckin' far ass hike.

00:07:55.150 --> 00:07:56.340
Believe me, I did it.

00:07:56.340 --> 00:07:59.550
We did it because we didn't
have no ride, nothin'.

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:02.850
A little ways there and this
old man in his RV and his wife

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:04.600
pull over to the side, gave us some water

00:08:04.600 --> 00:08:07.250
and told us we could hand on his RV

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:09.330
and get a ride to the RV place.

00:08:09.330 --> 00:08:10.950
And that's the like halfway.

00:08:10.950 --> 00:08:12.040
So, we drank water, whatever.

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:13.990
We get on this RV and we're all hangin' on

00:08:13.990 --> 00:08:16.020
and he gives us a ride
all the way over there.

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:17.850
So, we're halfway through our trip.

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:19.610
We're like maybe eight miles into it.

00:08:19.610 --> 00:08:21.210
I mean, this has taken it's toll, man.

00:08:21.210 --> 00:08:22.530
My legs are burning.

00:08:22.530 --> 00:08:23.363
You know what I mean?

00:08:23.363 --> 00:08:24.196
Constantly thirsty.

00:08:24.196 --> 00:08:25.500
And it's fuckin' hot over there.

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:26.717
You know what I mean?

00:08:26.717 --> 00:08:28.610
But when you're in Arizona
and you're there for awhile,

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:30.310
you become accustom to the heat.

00:08:30.310 --> 00:08:31.180
Like anywhere else.

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:32.418
You know what I mean?

00:08:32.418 --> 00:08:34.345
But the heat is so hot what we're in.

00:08:34.345 --> 00:08:35.178
I use to see my little cousins

00:08:35.178 --> 00:08:36.280
walkin' barefoot on the cement

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:38.210
and it's like 115 degrees.

00:08:38.210 --> 00:08:39.349
You know what I mean?

00:08:39.349 --> 00:08:42.030
I use to be like, man, their
feet must be fuckin' hard

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:43.710
or something because
it's really hot out here

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:45.090
and they're walkin' like nothin'.

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:46.510
But bein' that they live
there all their life

00:08:46.510 --> 00:08:48.900
I guess they become accustom to that heat.

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:50.740
You know, I try to put my
foot down on the cement.

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:51.720
Hell no.

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:53.280
You could fry an egg
on that fuckin' cement.

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:54.940
You know, and they're walkin'

00:08:54.940 --> 00:08:56.490
all the way to the market barefooted.

00:08:56.490 --> 00:08:57.323
You know what I mean?

00:08:57.323 --> 00:08:59.980
And that's pavement, inside,
walk rocks, everything.

00:08:59.980 --> 00:09:01.320
It ain't phasing them.

00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:02.930
So, you know, when I was in Arizona

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:04.410
we kinda got use to the heat,

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:07.820
so that was a little up from us walking.

00:09:07.820 --> 00:09:09.720
But we're about maybe a
quarter of a mile still,

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:11.320
a quarter of the way to go still

00:09:12.470 --> 00:09:13.400
and I'm thinkin', man, we
ain't gonna make it, man.

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:15.573
This shit's too fuckin' hot, man.

00:09:16.942 --> 00:09:18.490
Here comes one of the fellas, man.

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:19.970
He came from the school.

00:09:19.970 --> 00:09:20.803
He went to the border,

00:09:20.803 --> 00:09:21.636
seen it was closed,

00:09:21.636 --> 00:09:22.864
came back around,

00:09:22.864 --> 00:09:23.697
seen us walking.

00:09:23.697 --> 00:09:24.530
Went all the way down,

00:09:24.530 --> 00:09:25.363
turned around,

00:09:25.363 --> 00:09:26.560
came in and picked us up.

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:27.849
You know what I'm sayin'?

00:09:27.849 --> 00:09:28.682
He picked us up.

00:09:28.682 --> 00:09:29.515
Dude was only 13 years old.

00:09:29.515 --> 00:09:30.348
You know what I'm sayin'?

00:09:30.348 --> 00:09:31.181
I gave him his props.

00:09:31.181 --> 00:09:32.530
He was only 13 ,he came for us.

00:09:32.530 --> 00:09:34.100
You know, no one asked him.

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:35.540
No one told him shit.

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:36.373
You know what I mean?

00:09:36.373 --> 00:09:37.290
He ear hustled our conversation.

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:38.850
That's how he found out
where we were going.

00:09:38.850 --> 00:09:39.683
He wanted to go.

00:09:39.683 --> 00:09:42.011
He went and got a car and
everything so he could go

00:09:42.011 --> 00:09:42.844
and he was only 13.

00:09:42.844 --> 00:09:44.170
But when he came with the car, you know,

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:45.003
we were relieved.

00:09:45.003 --> 00:09:45.836
We're like, man, fuck.

00:09:45.836 --> 00:09:47.960
We each gave him a couple
hundred dollars each,

00:09:47.960 --> 00:09:49.480
you know, 'cause he came to pick us up

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:51.250
in the middle of nowhere, you know.

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:53.177
So, we get back over there

00:09:53.177 --> 00:09:54.620
and you know, you got,

00:09:54.620 --> 00:09:56.380
over there in Arizona,
you gotta understand that

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:58.560
they're not as quick as us.

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:00.960
They're not so adapt
to cars getting stolen.

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:02.244
You know what I'm saying?

00:10:02.244 --> 00:10:03.960
If something happens big,
comes out in the paper,

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:05.350
everybody's talkin' about it.

00:10:05.350 --> 00:10:06.950
Now, there's cars coming up missing

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:10.490
from those car lots, like,
four or five every other night.

00:10:10.490 --> 00:10:11.323
We're takin' em.

00:10:11.323 --> 00:10:12.710
We're just takin' 'em.

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:14.600
There's, oo shit,

00:10:14.600 --> 00:10:18.080
over there must be 20, 30 car lots.

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:19.276
You know what I mean?

00:10:19.276 --> 00:10:20.109
And they're all the same.

00:10:20.109 --> 00:10:21.030
It's all the same build.

00:10:21.030 --> 00:10:22.560
They're built all the same way.

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:23.600
You know, I don't understand.

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:26.040
That's not really burglary proof

00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:28.810
but bein' that we're over
there and it's a lot slower,

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:31.640
maybe they're not too
hip to lockin' that shit

00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:32.960
behind something where you can't get in.

00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:33.880
You know what I mean?

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:35.260
And they didn't do it.

00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:36.690
So, everywhere we went,

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:38.420
everywhere we went, man, they
like open the front door,

00:10:38.420 --> 00:10:39.890
I looked in, boom.

00:10:39.890 --> 00:10:41.010
Whole set of keys, man.

00:10:41.010 --> 00:10:42.610
Everywhere we went.

00:10:42.610 --> 00:10:43.443
We did that.

00:10:43.443 --> 00:10:44.810
We did that and

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:45.820
you know the reason I bring it up

00:10:45.820 --> 00:10:49.150
is because I was on a whole
different page with those dudes.

00:10:49.150 --> 00:10:51.620
There was no gang bangin' involved.

00:10:51.620 --> 00:10:52.760
I didn't have no enemies over there.

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:55.130
I mean, there was dudes
from hoods over there,

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:56.630
you know, and they were from LA hoods

00:10:56.630 --> 00:10:57.720
but they moved to Arizona.

00:10:57.720 --> 00:10:58.553
They started,

00:10:58.553 --> 00:10:59.630
came in Arizona.

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:01.130
You know, those dudes didn't say shit.

00:11:01.130 --> 00:11:03.880
It was more the dudes that came
from LA and went over there

00:11:03.880 --> 00:11:06.450
and transplanted over there in LA,

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:08.437
so like they're runnin'
something, you know.

00:11:08.437 --> 00:11:10.130
So, we got in shit with
'em a couple of times.

00:11:10.130 --> 00:11:11.227
You know what I mean?

00:11:11.227 --> 00:11:12.520
In front of the school, down
in their hood, you know.

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:14.160
But other than that, it was cool.

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:15.410
You know,I didn't have to worry

00:11:15.410 --> 00:11:17.730
about walkin' down the street over there

00:11:17.730 --> 00:11:18.563
and gettin' shot in the back.

00:11:18.563 --> 00:11:19.824
You know what I mean?

00:11:19.824 --> 00:11:21.160
I don't gotta look over
my shoulder, you know.

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:22.330
Right there you can drink beer.

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:23.163
You know what I mean?

00:11:23.163 --> 00:11:24.250
The cops don't really sweat shit.

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:25.535
You know what I mean?

00:11:25.535 --> 00:11:26.537
Like they sweat shit in LA, you know.

00:11:26.537 --> 00:11:28.190
And I was really comfortable
over there, you know,

00:11:28.190 --> 00:11:30.280
and I was thinkin', man,
I might just stay here.

00:11:30.280 --> 00:11:31.520
You know what I mean?

00:11:31.520 --> 00:11:32.353
And get a girlfriend.

00:11:32.353 --> 00:11:33.186
You know what I mean?

00:11:33.186 --> 00:11:34.750
And you know, raise a
family and just kick it.

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:36.727
But nah, it ain't happening.

00:11:36.727 --> 00:11:37.560
You know, it ain't happening.

00:11:37.560 --> 00:11:39.790
About shit, three weeks into my stay,

00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:41.030
phone call comes from the hood.

00:11:41.030 --> 00:11:42.251
You know what I mean?

00:11:42.251 --> 00:11:43.084
Hey, you gotta come back.

00:11:43.084 --> 00:11:44.210
You know what I mean?

00:11:44.210 --> 00:11:45.043
My little brother got out

00:11:45.043 --> 00:11:45.876
and he's running amuck.

00:11:45.876 --> 00:11:47.080
You know what I mean?

00:11:47.080 --> 00:11:48.310
I don't want him out there by himself.

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:50.180
So, I'm like, damn, how
am I gonna get back home?

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:51.013
You know what I mean?

00:11:51.013 --> 00:11:51.846
How am I gonna get back home?

00:11:51.846 --> 00:11:54.360
I'm thinkin' they Greyhound,
that's too fuckin' long, man.

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:55.300
That shit is too long.

00:11:55.300 --> 00:11:57.660
And I had some money on me
from the cars, you know.

00:11:57.660 --> 00:11:59.460
So, I got one of the neighbors,

00:11:59.460 --> 00:12:00.623
the white boy right there

00:12:00.623 --> 00:12:02.090
and I was like, hey man,
let's go to LA, you know.

00:12:02.090 --> 00:12:02.950
I'll take you over there with me.

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:03.783
We'll kick it.

00:12:03.783 --> 00:12:04.616
You know what I mean?

00:12:04.616 --> 00:12:05.500
You know a lot of my family.

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:06.470
We'll go over there and post up.

00:12:06.470 --> 00:12:08.160
He's like, man, that's a good idea.

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:09.020
Let's do it.

00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:09.853
So, fuck it.

00:12:09.853 --> 00:12:10.780
We loaded his car.

00:12:10.780 --> 00:12:12.470
We got in his car and
we drove all the way.

00:12:12.470 --> 00:12:15.140
Halfway there, his shit broke down

00:12:15.140 --> 00:12:16.060
in the middle of nowhere.

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:18.430
I'm talkin' about, just fuckin' mountains

00:12:18.430 --> 00:12:19.730
and fuckin' bushes.

00:12:19.730 --> 00:12:20.563
Nothin'.

00:12:20.563 --> 00:12:21.724
You know what I mean?

00:12:21.724 --> 00:12:22.557
Nothin'.

00:12:22.557 --> 00:12:23.390
Nobody stopping.

00:12:23.390 --> 00:12:24.223
Nobody stopping.

00:12:24.223 --> 00:12:25.670
All the sudden, here
some the highway patrol.

00:12:25.670 --> 00:12:27.430
That fool stopped, helped us.

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:29.210
We fixed the car and we got on, you know.

00:12:29.210 --> 00:12:31.150
Out of everybody, he stopped,

00:12:31.150 --> 00:12:31.983
the highway patrol.

00:12:31.983 --> 00:12:33.080
No on else was stopping, man.

00:12:33.080 --> 00:12:35.035
Mother fuckers were flyin' by.

00:12:35.035 --> 00:12:35.868
Zoom.

00:12:35.868 --> 00:12:36.701
Zoom.

00:12:36.701 --> 00:12:37.534
You know what I mean?

00:12:37.534 --> 00:12:38.367
I try and tell him, wait, you know.

00:12:38.367 --> 00:12:39.200
Fuck, help us out.

00:12:39.200 --> 00:12:40.033
Nobody.

00:12:40.033 --> 00:12:41.116
Nobody.

00:12:41.116 --> 00:12:41.949
And it's fuckin' hot.

00:12:41.949 --> 00:12:43.000
We're in the middle of the fuckin' desert.

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:45.570
We're like about 10 miles from Glamis.

00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:47.400
That's the fuckin' sand dunes,

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:49.020
you know, over there in that area.

00:12:49.020 --> 00:12:49.970
You know, it's the sand dunes

00:12:49.970 --> 00:12:51.410
and we're fuckin' just,

00:12:51.410 --> 00:12:52.620
we're stranded, man.

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:55.680
Well, he helps us out and
we get to a gas station.

00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:58.198
We call some heads, they come and get us

00:12:58.198 --> 00:12:59.670
but we're, you know, we're halfway there.

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:01.550
And you know, when they came and got us,

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:04.408
you know, we had some stuff
we brought from over there

00:13:04.408 --> 00:13:05.241
'cause you know, in Arizona, you know,

00:13:05.241 --> 00:13:08.240
you can do certain things
you can't do in California.

00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:10.100
You know, you can acquire certain things

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:11.750
you can't acquire in California.

00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:12.850
You could acquire 'em in Arizona.

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:14.230
It's a different law, you know.

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:16.610
I seen and old man walk into the store

00:13:16.610 --> 00:13:20.200
and he had two Colt 45 pistols on his lap

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:21.587
with a gang of bullets
like that, you know.

00:13:21.587 --> 00:13:23.640
And he was maybe like,

00:13:23.640 --> 00:13:25.560
he had to be at least 70, 80.

00:13:25.560 --> 00:13:26.393
You know what I mean?

00:13:26.393 --> 00:13:27.307
He had these two guns right there

00:13:27.307 --> 00:13:29.290
and he was walkin' down
the street like nothin'.

00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:31.569
And I was like, how the
fuck are you walkin' down,

00:13:31.569 --> 00:13:32.402
You know what I mean?

00:13:32.402 --> 00:13:33.470
With his guns like that.

00:13:33.470 --> 00:13:34.303
I said, I know he ain't no cop.

00:13:34.303 --> 00:13:35.660
He's kinda old to be a cop.

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:36.850
So, I asked the man at the store.

00:13:36.850 --> 00:13:38.710
I'm like, how does that guy
just come in here with guns?

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:40.700
He's like, well, Arizona law,

00:13:40.700 --> 00:13:43.760
you can brandish firearms
on you hips, you know.

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:45.810
You can have a firearm on your hip

00:13:45.810 --> 00:13:47.460
as long as its visible, and you know,

00:13:47.460 --> 00:13:48.650
you're showing it.

00:13:48.650 --> 00:13:49.483
You can have that.

00:13:49.483 --> 00:13:50.316
I didn't know that

00:13:50.316 --> 00:13:53.770
and then little by little I
started seeing more people

00:13:53.770 --> 00:13:54.780
strapped up, strapped up.

00:13:54.780 --> 00:13:57.982
I seen this dude had a
fuckin' belt buckle like this

00:13:57.982 --> 00:13:59.777
and it had a little ass gun
with like four bullets in it.

00:13:59.777 --> 00:14:01.500
And it was his belt buckle.

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:02.470
And it shot 22s.

00:14:02.470 --> 00:14:03.303
Little ass,

00:14:03.303 --> 00:14:05.021
little ass gun on his belt buckle.

00:14:05.021 --> 00:14:05.854
And you just push a button,

00:14:05.854 --> 00:14:06.860
that shit fall right in your hand.

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:07.750
I seen that one.

00:14:07.750 --> 00:14:10.788
That was right after I seen
that man with the Colt 45s

00:14:10.788 --> 00:14:11.621
'cause now I was interested.

00:14:11.621 --> 00:14:13.420
Me and Dan, while we were in Arizona,

00:14:13.420 --> 00:14:14.760
you could just buy 'em over the counter,

00:14:14.760 --> 00:14:16.540
like, fuck, we ain't
getting close over there.

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:18.277
So, I do my thing, you know,

00:14:18.277 --> 00:14:19.500
and they handle their business.

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:20.870
Like I was sayin', we got halfway there

00:14:20.870 --> 00:14:23.150
and that's what we're
really concerned about.

00:14:23.150 --> 00:14:24.250
When the highway patrol came,

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:25.170
we weren't really trippin'

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:26.020
because he was by himself

00:14:26.020 --> 00:14:27.430
and if he was gonna look through the car

00:14:27.430 --> 00:14:30.476
he had to look really good
where our hiding place was at

00:14:30.476 --> 00:14:31.340
you know, 'cause we made a hiding place

00:14:31.340 --> 00:14:33.990
where it's even hard for
us to fuckin' find it.

00:14:33.990 --> 00:14:35.020
You know what I mean?

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:36.320
So, we made it, you know.

00:14:36.320 --> 00:14:40.560
We get back to LA and as
soon as we get back to LA,

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:42.550
my little brother he's in jail.

00:14:42.550 --> 00:14:43.383
I'm like, what's he in jail for?

00:14:43.383 --> 00:14:45.380
Oh, he got busted for
a shooting last night.

00:14:45.380 --> 00:14:47.370
I said, I told him when I
called, I was coming the next day

00:14:47.370 --> 00:14:48.800
but he couldn't wait.

00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:50.060
You know, he was fresh outta jail.

00:14:50.060 --> 00:14:50.893
You know what I mean?

00:14:50.893 --> 00:14:52.240
And when you're fresh
outta jail, you know,

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:54.480
you got all that animosity built up,

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:56.890
all those fuckin' rumors you
hear about you girlfriend.

00:14:56.890 --> 00:14:58.104
You know what I mean?

00:14:58.104 --> 00:14:58.937
About your homeys.

00:14:58.937 --> 00:15:00.560
So, you might get out
there and smash everybody.

00:15:00.560 --> 00:15:01.884
You know what I mean?

00:15:01.884 --> 00:15:03.640
But I can honestly tell you the truth,

00:15:03.640 --> 00:15:06.150
there's not enough time
to smash everybody.

00:15:06.150 --> 00:15:07.414
You know what I mean?

00:15:07.414 --> 00:15:08.247
Everybody ain't worth it.

00:15:08.247 --> 00:15:10.150
Not all ass whoopin's are good, you know.

00:15:10.150 --> 00:15:11.536
You might whip a fool's ass

00:15:11.536 --> 00:15:12.540
and you know, he's gonna call the cops.

00:15:12.540 --> 00:15:15.560
You know, that's what I'm really
concerned about these days.

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:18.320
That, you know, oh, when I
was in Arizona, you know,

00:15:18.320 --> 00:15:20.160
they call the cops for beatin' up a dude

00:15:20.160 --> 00:15:23.030
and they just came, broke us up and left.

00:15:23.030 --> 00:15:25.780
Over here, I got busted
for beatin' up a dude.

00:15:25.780 --> 00:15:27.880
They arrested me, wanna
give me assault and battery.

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:30.050
And both of us were bleeding.

00:15:30.050 --> 00:15:31.840
But bein' that he called,

00:15:31.840 --> 00:15:32.780
you know what I mean?

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:33.640
He called 'em on me.

00:15:33.640 --> 00:15:34.650
He said I shoulda called

00:15:34.650 --> 00:15:36.300
but I'm not a cop caller.

00:15:36.300 --> 00:15:37.300
You know what I'm sayin'?

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:38.233
I can't do that.

00:15:39.150 --> 00:15:41.700
It's really hard for me to
call any law enforcement

00:15:41.700 --> 00:15:42.533
because of the fact

00:15:42.533 --> 00:15:45.060
that I just don't agree
with a lot of their tactics.

00:15:45.060 --> 00:15:46.130
You know, the things they do.

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:46.963
You know what I'm saying?

00:15:46.963 --> 00:15:48.235
I don't agree with them.

00:15:48.235 --> 00:15:49.068
You know what I mean?

00:15:49.068 --> 00:15:49.901
And right now they're off the chain,

00:15:49.901 --> 00:15:51.140
so I don't call 'em for nothin'.

00:15:51.140 --> 00:15:52.382
You know what I mean?

00:15:52.382 --> 00:15:53.690
And I like to get my camera and watch 'em

00:15:53.690 --> 00:15:55.180
'cause they're always
doin' some dumb shit.

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:56.013
You know what I mean?

00:15:56.013 --> 00:15:57.740
They're always doin' some dumb ass shit.

00:15:57.740 --> 00:15:59.990
But over there in Arizona, you know,

00:15:59.990 --> 00:16:03.380
but before I left, I
had got a can of paint

00:16:03.380 --> 00:16:04.800
and I started sniffin' paint.

00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:06.310
And when I was sniffin' paint,

00:16:06.310 --> 00:16:08.760
I thought my cousin was
tryin' to set me up.

00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:10.280
So, I ended up beatin' her up.

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:12.170
The cops came, arrest me,

00:16:12.170 --> 00:16:14.390
take me to jail, put me in juvenile hall

00:16:14.390 --> 00:16:16.430
and the one thing I remember
about that juvenile hall

00:16:16.430 --> 00:16:17.650
is when you get there,

00:16:17.650 --> 00:16:20.050
they got this thing called adjustment.

00:16:20.050 --> 00:16:22.900
For a whole day, you
have to sit in your room,

00:16:22.900 --> 00:16:24.473
with your mattress rolled up.

00:16:25.340 --> 00:16:26.173
Your water, food, whatever.

00:16:26.173 --> 00:16:27.530
But you can't lay down

00:16:27.530 --> 00:16:28.530
for a whole day.

00:16:28.530 --> 00:16:31.060
And this is in Arizona juvenile hall.

00:16:31.060 --> 00:16:32.370
You know, they don't let you sit down

00:16:32.370 --> 00:16:33.620
for a whole fuckin' day.

00:16:33.620 --> 00:16:34.870
And I didn't understand that.

00:16:34.870 --> 00:16:36.040
You know, that's like in humane.

00:16:36.040 --> 00:16:36.873
You know.

00:16:36.873 --> 00:16:37.760
You can use the bathroom, you know,

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:38.890
but you had to stay sitting there.

00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:41.140
You couldn't lay down,
close your eyes, you know,

00:16:41.140 --> 00:16:41.973
they'd bang on your door.

00:16:41.973 --> 00:16:43.240
Bam, bam, bam.

00:16:43.240 --> 00:16:44.073
You know what I mean?

00:16:44.073 --> 00:16:45.500
And I was like, how the
fuck does that work,

00:16:45.500 --> 00:16:46.690
adjustment for a child.

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:47.852
You know what I mean?

00:16:47.852 --> 00:16:50.200
So, you know, Arizona has
its good and its bads.

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:51.380
You know.

00:16:51.380 --> 00:16:52.470
Arizona, you do something,

00:16:52.470 --> 00:16:53.660
you rob a liquor store,

00:16:53.660 --> 00:16:55.920
they give you like, 27 years, man

00:16:55.920 --> 00:16:57.940
but you'll only be doin' like six, seven.

00:16:57.940 --> 00:17:00.470
But they give you this way
out number, like 56 years.

00:17:00.470 --> 00:17:02.480
You see a dude out in like five years.

00:17:02.480 --> 00:17:03.313
You know what I mean?

00:17:03.313 --> 00:17:04.370
Their laws are different than us.

00:17:04.370 --> 00:17:05.203
You know what I mean?

00:17:05.203 --> 00:17:06.260
They run their shit different.

00:17:06.260 --> 00:17:08.090
You know, everything.

00:17:08.090 --> 00:17:09.560
Their IDs look different.

00:17:09.560 --> 00:17:11.023
Everything is,

00:17:12.163 --> 00:17:13.720
it's more like a western
shit that I notice.

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:16.080
They got more like a
different heritage back then,

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:17.510
behind them, you know.

00:17:17.510 --> 00:17:18.343
I use to go,

00:17:18.343 --> 00:17:19.890
oh, we use to ditch school

00:17:19.890 --> 00:17:21.050
and I remember when I was in high school,

00:17:21.050 --> 00:17:21.883
we use to ditch school,

00:17:21.883 --> 00:17:23.776
like 15 of us.

00:17:23.776 --> 00:17:24.740
And we would go to the Colorado River.

00:17:24.740 --> 00:17:26.930
It was like three blocks
away from the high school.

00:17:26.930 --> 00:17:28.700
So, we'll go and we'll take plastic bags

00:17:28.700 --> 00:17:30.990
and when the truant officers
and the cops would come,

00:17:30.990 --> 00:17:34.057
we'd just jump in the water
and swim to the other side

00:17:34.057 --> 00:17:34.890
and get out over there

00:17:34.890 --> 00:17:35.770
and fuck you, you know.

00:17:35.770 --> 00:17:36.850
They can't come on that side.

00:17:36.850 --> 00:17:38.180
It's not their jurisdiction.

00:17:38.180 --> 00:17:39.780
That's California, you know.

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:41.240
And so, we'd go back and forth.

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:42.442
You know what I mean?

00:17:42.442 --> 00:17:43.275
And fuck with the cops.

00:17:43.275 --> 00:17:44.108
And the only ones we
didn't really fuck with

00:17:44.108 --> 00:17:45.930
was the fuckin' border patrol

00:17:45.930 --> 00:17:47.200
'cause those fools don't give a fuck.

00:17:47.200 --> 00:17:48.580
They'll go anywhere,
on any side, you know,

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:50.010
in the water, they'll come and get you.

00:17:50.010 --> 00:17:51.350
They have, believe me.

00:17:51.350 --> 00:17:52.620
So, we were doin' that for awhile.

00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:53.453
We were ditching.

00:17:53.453 --> 00:17:54.660
And because we were ditching,

00:17:54.660 --> 00:17:56.500
more and more people were finding out,

00:17:56.500 --> 00:17:59.150
so i think at the last
ditch it party that we had,

00:17:59.150 --> 00:18:02.130
that we musta had like
50, 60 people there.

00:18:02.130 --> 00:18:03.370
And the cops came and raided.

00:18:03.370 --> 00:18:04.320
Truant officers, everything.

00:18:04.320 --> 00:18:06.660
A lot of people got in trouble.

00:18:06.660 --> 00:18:07.960
And the whole thing, you know,

00:18:07.960 --> 00:18:09.550
what I hated about the situation

00:18:09.550 --> 00:18:11.370
is when they all got in trouble,

00:18:11.370 --> 00:18:12.953
all their fingers went,

00:18:12.953 --> 00:18:14.060
(exhales sharply)

00:18:14.060 --> 00:18:14.893
to me.

00:18:14.893 --> 00:18:16.671
You know, they all pointed to me.

00:18:16.671 --> 00:18:17.504
And you know, and I kinda figured it

00:18:17.504 --> 00:18:19.460
because they weren't doin'
nothin' like that over there.

00:18:19.460 --> 00:18:21.150
They weren't stealin' no cars.

00:18:21.150 --> 00:18:22.310
They weren't fuckin' jumping people.

00:18:22.310 --> 00:18:23.596
They weren't doin' that.

00:18:23.596 --> 00:18:24.790
They were just goin' to school.

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:26.540
They're fuckin' thing
was to go to the arcade

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:27.480
or you know,

00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:30.150
go fuckin' play in an
abandoned building, you know.

00:18:30.150 --> 00:18:32.160
They didn't know nothin'
about us go take some cars,

00:18:32.160 --> 00:18:34.550
drive 'em over here and you
thousands in your pockets.

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:36.675
So, a lot of those dudes
that I did that with,

00:18:36.675 --> 00:18:38.060
you know, a lot of 'em now are in jail.

00:18:38.060 --> 00:18:39.520
You know, I talk to a couple of 'em.

00:18:39.520 --> 00:18:41.610
You know, maybe they're
still doin' their thing.

00:18:41.610 --> 00:18:42.790
But I kinda feel bad 'cause you know,

00:18:42.790 --> 00:18:46.210
I kinda started 'em off on that bad trail.

00:18:46.210 --> 00:18:47.190
You know what I mean?

00:18:47.190 --> 00:18:48.650
But I let 'em know, you
don't gotta come with me.

00:18:48.650 --> 00:18:49.483
I'll go myself.

00:18:49.483 --> 00:18:50.890
I'll just come pick you
up afterward with girls.

00:18:50.890 --> 00:18:52.360
But no, they wanna go.

00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:53.470
They wanna take their own car.

00:18:53.470 --> 00:18:54.303
They wanna look cool.

00:18:54.303 --> 00:18:55.370
Okay, go ahead, you know.

00:18:55.370 --> 00:18:58.810
So, a few of them, I know,
went to jail behind that.

00:18:58.810 --> 00:19:00.050
Behind fingerprints.

00:19:00.050 --> 00:19:01.160
'Cause remember, I just got there,

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:03.020
so, they didn't have me down on file.

00:19:03.020 --> 00:19:04.570
Those fools, though, they went to jail.

00:19:04.570 --> 00:19:06.040
Cops came to their house,

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:07.490
raided their shit,

00:19:07.490 --> 00:19:08.650
took all their dad's guns,

00:19:08.650 --> 00:19:09.483
took their guns,

00:19:09.483 --> 00:19:10.590
fuckin' took everything.

00:19:10.590 --> 00:19:11.423
You know what I mean?

00:19:11.423 --> 00:19:12.880
And took them to jail, you know.

00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:14.600
And what was crazy was,

00:19:14.600 --> 00:19:16.800
they got booked for other shit

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:18.380
that I knew nothing about.

00:19:18.380 --> 00:19:20.390
And it was suppose to
be all of us together.

00:19:20.390 --> 00:19:22.760
So, these fools were
pulling some slick shit

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:24.130
and they got caught up

00:19:24.130 --> 00:19:25.720
because they pulled slick shit, you know.

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:27.970
But you know, I wanted
to show you a day about,

00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:30.130
I'm always talkin' about
here in LA, you know.

00:19:30.130 --> 00:19:31.590
But it's anywhere you go, you know.

00:19:31.590 --> 00:19:34.590
Anywhere you go, if you're
part of a certain environment,

00:19:34.590 --> 00:19:37.420
you're gonna find where
those people are, you know.

00:19:37.420 --> 00:19:38.610
If you wanna get high,

00:19:38.610 --> 00:19:40.454
you're gonna look so long,

00:19:40.454 --> 00:19:41.780
that you're gonna eventually see someone

00:19:41.780 --> 00:19:44.250
that's doing the movement or something

00:19:44.250 --> 00:19:45.440
of someone who's high.

00:19:45.440 --> 00:19:46.630
So many places I've been,

00:19:46.630 --> 00:19:48.900
when I got to Arizona,
the first dude I asked,

00:19:48.900 --> 00:19:50.240
hell yeah, he knew
where to get everything.

00:19:50.240 --> 00:19:51.469
You know what I mean?

00:19:51.469 --> 00:19:53.470
And you know, I've had that
happen to me a lot here in LA.

00:19:53.470 --> 00:19:56.560
You know, big truck drivers
and shit would pull over

00:19:56.560 --> 00:19:57.480
and come and hit at me

00:19:57.480 --> 00:19:58.970
and be like, hey man, can you hook me up?

00:19:58.970 --> 00:20:00.450
I'm all the way from Kentucky.

00:20:00.450 --> 00:20:01.350
I'm just comin' through.

00:20:01.350 --> 00:20:02.600
This is a stop, you know.

00:20:04.101 --> 00:20:05.570
And I'm thinkin', man, I
don't wanna hook this fool up.

00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:06.900
But damn, once he says, hey man,

00:20:06.900 --> 00:20:08.230
I'll give you $200 for yourself.

00:20:08.230 --> 00:20:09.430
Now, what the fuck?

00:20:09.430 --> 00:20:10.858
Just for pickin' up for him,

00:20:10.858 --> 00:20:12.000
you're gonna give me 200 bucks?

00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:13.280
And that's not just what he's giving.

00:20:13.280 --> 00:20:14.790
He's only giving me
that from the beginning.

00:20:14.790 --> 00:20:16.220
This is not when I bring him back the shit

00:20:16.220 --> 00:20:17.110
and he sees it's a lot.

00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:17.943
He's happy now.

00:20:17.943 --> 00:20:19.630
So, he breaks me off another 40, you know.

00:20:19.630 --> 00:20:21.590
And then before I leave, another 40.

00:20:21.590 --> 00:20:24.380
So, you know, the fool breaks
me off three, 400, $500.

00:20:24.380 --> 00:20:27.690
And it's happened like
maybe seven, eight times

00:20:27.690 --> 00:20:28.880
right here in Los Angeles.

00:20:28.880 --> 00:20:30.370
And I'm just walkin' down the street.

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:31.750
Been approached by women,

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:33.090
a man, a man and women,

00:20:33.090 --> 00:20:34.570
and they're all truck drivers, you know.

00:20:34.570 --> 00:20:39.070
And I'm wondering, why would they ask me?

00:20:39.070 --> 00:20:43.400
You know, what aura or what do I give off

00:20:43.400 --> 00:20:46.080
saying that I would know
where to find drugs?

00:20:46.080 --> 00:20:49.270
You know, even if I'm just
walkin' down the street,

00:20:49.270 --> 00:20:51.500
I know they can't see that
I'm high and I'm on drugs.

00:20:51.500 --> 00:20:52.333
They can't.

00:20:52.333 --> 00:20:55.070
But I mean, it's just
so bad that, you know,

00:20:55.070 --> 00:20:58.090
people from another
state, cruisin' through,

00:20:58.090 --> 00:21:00.510
stop me to buy them drugs, you know.

00:21:00.510 --> 00:21:02.650
And I'm like, okay,
what do I gotta change?

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:04.750
Do I gotta change my attire?

00:21:04.750 --> 00:21:06.470
Do I gotta change my appearance more?

00:21:06.470 --> 00:21:07.627
You know, I'm almost 50 years old

00:21:07.627 --> 00:21:09.577
and I'm tired of
youngsters mad doggin' me,

00:21:09.577 --> 00:21:11.270
askin' me where I'm from.

00:21:11.270 --> 00:21:12.411
You know what I mean?

00:21:12.411 --> 00:21:14.050
And it's like 22 year old, 21 year old kid

00:21:14.050 --> 00:21:14.883
askin' me where I'm from.

00:21:14.883 --> 00:21:16.490
I'm almost 50 years old.

00:21:16.490 --> 00:21:17.323
So, a lot of times,

00:21:17.323 --> 00:21:19.670
I just wanna bend 'em over and spank 'em.

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:21.810
But then again, I knew I was
like that before, you know.

00:21:21.810 --> 00:21:24.260
I was at that age, you know.

00:21:24.260 --> 00:21:26.439
But I wanna share that with
you this time, you know,

00:21:26.439 --> 00:21:27.272
about,

00:21:27.272 --> 00:21:28.420
it don't matter where you go, man.

00:21:28.420 --> 00:21:30.940
It's not just here in
Los Angeles and Skid Row.

00:21:30.940 --> 00:21:32.250
It's everywhere, you know.

00:21:32.250 --> 00:21:34.310
I've been from one tip of California

00:21:34.310 --> 00:21:35.630
all the way to the other side

00:21:35.630 --> 00:21:40.630
and every fuckin' city has
a ghetto, a slum, the hood.

00:21:40.630 --> 00:21:42.140
You know, I've been places where they got,

00:21:42.140 --> 00:21:46.480
actually got rows and rows of
what they call, slam shacks.

00:21:46.480 --> 00:21:49.270
They're abandoned houses up on stilts

00:21:49.270 --> 00:21:51.070
and all the people go in
there and slam in there,

00:21:51.070 --> 00:21:51.903
live in there.

00:21:51.903 --> 00:21:53.766
You know, there's no landlord.

00:21:53.766 --> 00:21:54.599
There's no nothin'.

00:21:54.599 --> 00:21:56.430
It's just rows and rows of empty houses.

00:21:56.430 --> 00:21:57.263
And it's a trip

00:21:57.263 --> 00:21:59.050
because I remember when
I first went in there.

00:21:59.050 --> 00:22:00.290
It's a regular house

00:22:00.290 --> 00:22:02.210
but it's called a slam shack.

00:22:02.210 --> 00:22:04.380
And they got like 15 on this side,

00:22:04.380 --> 00:22:05.290
10 on that side,

00:22:05.290 --> 00:22:06.520
five on that side.

00:22:06.520 --> 00:22:07.780
I've never ever seen it there.

00:22:07.780 --> 00:22:10.850
The only place I've ever seen
it was Madera, California.

00:22:10.850 --> 00:22:13.500
In Madera, California they have
what they call slam shacks.

00:22:13.500 --> 00:22:14.333
And they're crazy

00:22:14.333 --> 00:22:16.245
because everything in there.

00:22:16.245 --> 00:22:18.260
There's a range of all kinds
of shit everywhere, you know.

00:22:18.260 --> 00:22:20.130
The cops never go in there.

00:22:20.130 --> 00:22:20.963
You know what I mean?

00:22:20.963 --> 00:22:21.796
And I was like, whoa, you know.

00:22:21.796 --> 00:22:25.960
So, every place has a place
where you can find trouble.

00:22:25.960 --> 00:22:26.960
That's what I'm sayin', you know.

00:22:26.960 --> 00:22:29.250
And if you don't go to find trouble,

00:22:29.250 --> 00:22:30.083
trouble'll find you.

00:22:30.083 --> 00:22:31.750
Trouble always finds me wherever I go.

00:22:31.750 --> 00:22:34.510
I ended up leavin' Arizona
'cause I had to leave.

00:22:34.510 --> 00:22:36.367
Cops were already on our tail and shit.

00:22:36.367 --> 00:22:37.570
They were already booking all these fools.

